Tool Look for Means <code>uptime</code> load &gt; #CPUs and rising Saturation building <code>dmesg -T</code> <code>Out of memory</code>, <code>blocked for 120s</code>, <code>Link is Down</code> Hard event already happened <code>vmstat</code> <code>wa</code> high I/O wait. <code>st</code> high = hypervisor steal <code>vmstat</code> <code>si/so</code> non-zero Swapping — RAM is over <code>mpstat</code> one CPU 100%, others idle Single-threaded bottleneck or IRQ pinned <code>pidstat</code> %CPU &gt; 100 = multi-thread offender Found the process <code>iostat -xz</code> <code>%util</code> 100, <code>await</code> &gt;&gt; <code>svctm</code> Disk saturated, queue backed up <code>free -m</code> <code>available</code> &lt; 10% of total Cache pressure <code>sar -n DEV</code> rxerr/txerr/drop &gt; 0 NIC layer problem <code>sar -n ETCP</code> retrans/s rising Network or peer overload Mermaid source <pre><code>flowchart TD
  Start([Incident page]) --&gt; Sixty[Run 60s checklist]
  Sixty --&gt; Q1{wa or st high?}
  Q1 --&gt;|yes| IO[io-issues.md / cpu-issues.md steal]
  Q1 --&gt;|no| Q2{si/so or OOM?}
  Q2 --&gt;|yes| MEM[memory-issues.md]
  Q2 --&gt;|no| Q3{retrans/drops?}
  Q3 --&gt;|yes| NET[network-issues.md]
  Q3 --&gt;|no| Q4{kernel msgs panic/lockup?}
  Q4 --&gt;|yes| KER[kernel-panic-and-debug.md]
  Q4 --&gt;|no| APP[application-debug.md]
</code></pre>

Mermaid source <pre><code>flowchart TD
  S[High CPU symptom] --&gt; Q1{vmstat 'st' &gt; 5%?}
  Q1 --&gt;|yes| HV[Hypervisor steal — noisy neighbour]
  Q1 --&gt;|no| Q2{mpstat: one CPU pegged?}
  Q2 --&gt;|yes| Q3{which is hot?}
  Q3 --&gt;|%sy high| KER[Kernel hot path / IRQ storm]
  Q3 --&gt;|%us high| APP[Single-thread app or hot loop]
  Q3 --&gt;|%si high| SOFTIRQ[Network softirq — see network-issues.md]
  Q2 --&gt;|no, all CPUs busy| Q4{cgroup throttling?}
  Q4 --&gt;|nr_throttled rising| CG[cgroup cpu cap]
  Q4 --&gt;|no| Q5{perf top hot function?}
  Q5 --&gt;|kernel sym| KER
  Q5 --&gt;|app sym| APP
  Q5 --&gt;|spinlock_*| LOCK[Lock contention]
</code></pre>

Mermaid source <pre><code>flowchart TD
  S[Slow I/O] --&gt; Q1{iostat 'await' &gt; 20ms?}
  Q1 --&gt;|yes| Q2{which device?}
  Q2 --&gt;|root /| ROOT[Log volume? Swap?]
  Q2 --&gt;|data vol| DAT[App workload]
  Q2 --&gt;|all| BACK[Backplane / SAN issue]
  Q1 --&gt;|no| Q3{wa high but await low?}
  Q3 --&gt;|yes| FS[Filesystem locks / journal]
  Q1 --&gt;|no| Q4{df -i full?}
  Q4 --&gt;|yes| INODE[Inode exhaustion]
  Q4 --&gt;|no| Q5{dmesg I/O errors?}
  Q5 --&gt;|yes| HW2[Hardware / cable / SMART]
  Q5 --&gt;|no| APP2[App-level fsync flood]
</code></pre>

Mermaid source <pre><code>flowchart TD
  S[Memory symptom] --&gt; Q1{dmesg shows OOM?}
  Q1 --&gt;|yes| Q2{memcg or global?}
  Q2 --&gt;|memcg killed| CG[cgroup limit too low or leak]
  Q2 --&gt;|global oom| GLO[Host RAM exhausted]
  Q1 --&gt;|no| Q3{si/so non-zero?}
  Q3 --&gt;|yes| SW[Swap thrashing]
  Q3 --&gt;|no| Q4{available &lt; 10%?}
  Q4 --&gt;|yes, slab huge| SLAB[Slab cache bloat]
  Q4 --&gt;|yes, RSS growing| LEAK[App leak]
  Q4 --&gt;|no, but latency spikes| THP[THP defrag stalls]
</code></pre>

Mermaid source <pre><code>flowchart TD
  S[Network symptom] --&gt; Q1{ping ok, tcp not?}
  Q1 --&gt;|yes| MTU[MTU mismatch / PMTUD black hole]
  Q1 --&gt;|no, ping fails| L3[Routing / firewall / ARP]
  Q1 --&gt;|tcp ok intermittent| Q2{ss -s many time-wait?}
  Q2 --&gt;|yes| TW[TIME_WAIT or port exhaustion]
  Q2 --&gt;|no| Q3{nstat retrans rising?}
  Q3 --&gt;|yes| LOSS[Packet loss upstream]
  Q3 --&gt;|no| Q4{dmesg conntrack full?}
  Q4 --&gt;|yes| CT[Conntrack table full]
  Q4 --&gt;|no| Q5{ifconfig errors/drops?}
  Q5 --&gt;|yes| NIC2[NIC ring / driver / cable]
  Q5 --&gt;|no| APP3[Application timeouts]
</code></pre>

Concept Manifest / Snippet Command Expected output <p>Each container has its own network namespace, glued together by Docker bridges. The default <code>bridge</code> has no DNS between containers — always create a user-defined bridge so services can resolve each other by name.</p> <pre><code># compose.yaml fragment — user-defined bridge with DNS
services:
  api:    { image: myapi,    networks: [app-net] }
  worker: { image: myworker, networks: [app-net] }
networks:
  app-net:
    driver: bridge
</code></pre> <pre><code>docker network create demo-net
docker run -d --name web --network demo-net nginx:1.27-alpine
docker run --rm --network demo-net alpine \
  sh -c 'apk add --no-cache curl &gt;/dev/null &amp;&amp; curl -s http://web | head -1'
docker network inspect demo-net
</code></pre> <pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
"Subnet":  "172.18.0.0/16"
"Gateway": "172.18.0.1"
"Containers": {
  "&lt;id&gt;": { "Name": "web", "IPv4Address": "172.18.0.2/16" }
}
</code></pre>

Mermaid source <pre><code>flowchart TD
  Q[What are you running?] --&gt; S{Stateless?}
  S --&gt;|Yes| D[Deployment]
  S --&gt;|No, needs identity/storage| ST[StatefulSet]
  Q --&gt; N{One per node?}
  N --&gt;|Yes| DS[DaemonSet]
  Q --&gt; B{Run-to-completion?}
  B --&gt;|Once| J[Job]
